<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sea of Galilee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sea of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> is a freshwater lake in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, fed by the Jordan River. In 1187 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s forces manoeuvred the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> army into waterless terrain nearby and denied it access to the lake. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> describe the resulting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Battle of Hattin</a> as a total Ayyubid victory that opened the way to the recapture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sea-of-galilee.jpg" alt="Sea of Galilee" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zachi Evenor and User:MathKnight · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinneret_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
